 TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIZAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARAGUCHI, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKASHIMA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENOO, KIKUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIZAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for producing a square cell by welding a sealing plate to the periphery of the opening of a square case containing a power generating element by a laser beam to seal the square case.  A sealing plate (2) is placed on an upper opening of a square case (1).  The sealing plate (2) has the same shape as that of the opening.  A laser beam (3a to 3d) is applied at a downward angle to the sides (a to d) including the corner (e) of a contact line (4) and is scanned along the contact line (4) to seal the opening of the case with the sealing plate.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de produire une pile rectangulaire par soudage d'une plaque de scellement à la périphérie de l'ouverture d'un conteneur rectangulaire contenant un élément de production d'énergie, ce soudage étant effectué à l'aide d'un faisceau laser destiné à sceller ledit conteneur. Ce procédé consiste tout d'abord à placer une plaque de scellement (2) sur l'ouverture supérieure du conteneur rectangulaire (1), cette plaque de scellement (2) présentant la même forme que celle de ladite ouverture. Ce procédé consiste ensuite à appliquer un faisceau laser (3a à 3d) sur un angle inférieur par rapport aux côtés (a à d), et notamment le coin e), d'une ligne de contact (4), puis à balayer ce faisceau le long de cette ligne de contact (4) afin de sceller l'ouverture dudit conteneur au moyen de la plaque de scellement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>